# Security Audit (rpi-yolo26-sandbox)

Invoke with `@security-audit`. Run checks; report pass/fail. Skip generic web auth.

**Scope:** repo hygiene before push to GitHub

## Repo (run these)

```sh
# Deps (skip if no .venv or no requirements yet)
test -f .venv/bin/activate && test -f requirements.txt -o -f requirements/ -o -f pyproject.toml && \
  . .venv/bin/activate && pip-audit

git status --short
git diff --cached --name-only
git ls-files

# Secrets and credential-shaped strings (ignore local-only trees)
rg -i 'BEGIN (RSA |OPENSSH |EC |DSA )?PRIVATE KEY|api[_-]?key|secret[_-]?key|password\s*[=:]|smtp[_-]?pass|app[_-]?password|AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}|ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|hf_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|xox[baprs]-' \
  --glob '!notes/**' --glob '!.venv/**' --glob '!.git/**' .

# Email / SMTP wiring must use env or placeholders, not live secrets
rg -i 'smtp|mail_|sendgrid|ses_|email.*(pass|user|host)|MAIL_' \
  --glob '!notes/**' --glob '!.venv/**' --glob '!.git/**' \
  -g '*.py' -g '*.yaml' -g '*.yml' -g '*.env*' -g '*.service' -g '*.md'
```

**Staged or tracked files must not include:**

| Path / pattern | Why |
|---|---|
| `.env`, `.env.*` (except `.env.example` with placeholders) | SMTP, API, local secrets |
| `credentials*.md`, `*secret*`, `*password*` | Credential dumps |
| `*.pem`, `*.key`, `id_rsa*`, `*.ppk`, `otp.bin` | Keys / tokens |
| `notes/` | Local-only research and host details |
| Capture images (`*.jpg`, `*.jpeg`, `*.png`, `*.webp`) | Field/trap imagery |
| `logs/`, `*.log`, `*.jsonl` | Runtime paths, system info |
| Model binaries (`*.pt`, `*.pth`, `*.onnx`, `*.tflite`, `*.engine`, `*_ncnn_model/`, `*_openvino_model/`) | Large / proprietary weights |
| `.venv/` | Local env |

Confirm `.gitignore` still covers the rows above. Fail if a forbidden path is staged or already tracked (`git ls-files`).

## Project-specific (confirm; no shell unless asked)

- **Email alerts:** SMTP user/password, app passwords, and API mail tokens live in `.env` or Pi-local config only. Committed `config.yaml` / examples use placeholders.
- **Recipient addresses:** OK in examples if non-sensitive; do not commit personal inboxes with credentials.
- **Pi access:** no SSH private keys, `authorized_keys` private material, WiFi PSK, or LAN host/IP inventory in git.
- **systemd units:** no `Environment=` lines with live passwords; reference env files outside the repo or `.env` (gitignored).
- **Dashboard / bind:** if a local review server exists, bind `127.0.0.1` only unless the user explicitly wants LAN exposure.
- **Absolute Mac/Pi home paths** in committed docs: prefer relative or generic paths; strip personal usernames when avoidable.

## Pass / fail

| Fail | Action |
|---|---|
| Secret or credential hit in staged/tracked content | Stop; do not push |
| Forbidden path staged or tracked | Unstage / untrack; stop |
| Live SMTP/SSH/WiFi secret in config or unit file | Stop; move to `.env` |
| `pip-audit` critical unmitigated (when run) | Stop or document accepted exception |

On **pass**, state: *Security audit passed this session.*
